<title>UK: Coutts Consulting drops on profit warning.</title>
<headline>Coutts Consulting drops on profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Coutts Consulting Group Plc dropped on Wednesday after the training and career counselling company warned of a shortfall in first-half profits.</p>
<p>Speaking at the company's annual meeting, chairman Stephen Johnson said earnings in the first half of the current year would be &quot;significantly below the same period last year.&quot;</p>
<p>He said the career consultation business was consolidating worldwide and Coutts was reviewing its operations with the intention of focusing on its core activities.</p>
<p>The stock closed 12p lower at 35-1/2.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
